# ai.wing — running changelog

Every change to this project gets an entry: date, what changed, files touched, why.
Newest first.

---

## 2026-08-19 — Fix: final CTA button thrown to the section edge

**What changed**

`FinalCta`'s `.formWrap` was `display: flex; justify-content: center`. That was right when it
wrapped a single `<AddressCheck>`. The call-primary rework earlier today put **two** children
inside it — the call button and the hours/routing line — so the flex row laid them side by side
and shoved the button out to the left edge of the section while the meta text ran on beside it.
Everything else in the section is centred, so it read as broken layout.

Changed to `flex-direction: column; align-items: center`, which stacks and centres them. Also
capped `.callMeta` at `46ch` so the routing sentence wraps into a readable block under the
button instead of running the full section width.

Worth remembering: this wrapper is styled for its *children*, not for itself. Adding a third
child to `.formWrap` will need the same look.

**Files touched**
`src/components/sections/FinalCta.module.css`.

**Verified**
Button, meta line and ZIP toggle all measure 0px offset from the section centre at 1440 / 768 /
390, stacked in that order. `tsc` clean; `lint-copy` clean; static export builds 18 routes;
0 horizontal overflow across 10 routes x 5 widths.

