## 2026-08-19 — §2.1 header logo swap; §4 strip confirmed final

**What changed**

**Fix 1 — carrier wordmark out of the header (§2.1)**

New `OperatorMark` replaces `RiseLogo` in `SiteHeader`. The `Authorized / Reseller` tag that sat
beside it is gone too — that association belongs in the §2.0 disclosure bar directly above, which
states it in words and is left byte-for-byte unchanged.

§2.1 bans carrier logos *and carrier-logo-derived marks*. "Derived" is the constraint that
actually shapes this component: recolouring the carrier mark, simplifying it, or rebuilding it in
the same typographic register all still read as the carrier's identity. So `OperatorMark` shares
nothing with Rise Internet's mark by construction:

- **No orange.** Rise's mark is defined by its brand orange, so this one is monochrome and
  inherits `color` from its parent. `OperatorMark.module.css` must never reference the ember
  ramp — a recoloured carrier mark is still a carrier mark. There is a comment at the top of the
  file saying so.
- **No bolt, no stacked word-over-rule lockup.** Those two shapes *are* the Rise mark. This is an
  upright bordered monogram tile on a single baseline. The tile is squared (0.28em), deliberately
  not the pill radius every CTA on the site uses.
- **Different face.** Rise's wordmark is the condensed display face in caps; this is the
  normal-width text face in sentence case, with weight contrast (700/400) carrying the lockup in
  place of a decorative glyph.

Content derives from `site.brandName` — initials for the tile, first word bold and the remainder
light. Falls back to a neutral `Operator` placeholder if the entity is unset. It must never
render empty and must never silently fall back to the carrier's name.

`tone="auto"` is retained, so the mark still cross-fades white-over-hero to ink-over-solid-bar on
the header's existing scrolled transition.

**Header height did not change**, which was the specific risk flagged: 140 / 125 / 105 / 106 /
118px at 360 / 390 / 480–900 / 1024 / 1440. The disclosure bar still wraps to three lines at
360px and two at 390px, and the hero's flat `8.5rem` / `10rem` mobile padding still clears it —
gap to the hero eyebrow is 54px at 360px, 69px at 390px, never negative. The `data-scrolled`
white-bar state was re-checked separately; the mark reads correctly in both.

Brand link is 44×148px at 360px with 132px of clearance to the burger.

**Related bug fixed in the footer.** The footer's `RiseLogo` was passing
`label={site.resellerName}`, which after this session's entity rename resolves to `Peak Connect`
— so a screen reader announced "Peak Connect" over Rise Internet glyphs. Now labelled
`site.carrierName`. The footer keeps the carrier mark deliberately: it is used there under
authorization, tagged "Authorized Reseller", directly above the operator's legal entity and the
§7.5 attribution line. §2.1's ban is header-scoped.

**Fix 2 — §4 strip confirmed final, no restoration**

Audited for dead code. No component files for the banned effects remain — mesh gradient, mouse
parallax, glowing dots and network patterns were fully deleted in the previous pass, not merely
unmounted. Also verified: no orphaned `.module.css` without a matching `.tsx`, and no unmounted
components anywhere in `src/components`.

Two stale comments corrected. These matter more than they look — both described behaviour that
no longer exists, in the present tense, which is exactly how a future edit gets misled:

- `globals.css` claimed "Lenis applies its own offset for same-page clicks", implying the
  `scroll-margin-top` rule only mattered for cross-route hashes. Scrolling is entirely native now
  and the rule applies to both.
- `trust.ts` called `marqueeItems` a "Marquee payload". It renders as a static wrapped list. The
  export name is kept — it is referenced across the trust band and its contents never depended on
  the presentation — but the comment now says so explicitly.

The three remaining mentions of removed libraries in `src` are intentional past-tense notes
explaining *why* something was removed, and should stay.

**Files touched**
`src/components/brand/OperatorMark.tsx` + `.module.css` (new),
`src/components/layout/SiteHeader.tsx` + `.module.css` (mark swapped, `.resellerTag` rules
removed including the 640px override), `src/components/layout/SiteFooter.tsx` (logo label),
`src/app/globals.css` and `src/lib/trust.ts` (stale comments).

`RiseLogo` is retained — still used by the footer.

**Not touched, per instruction:** `site.ts` TFN, entity name, address and email. Those still need
real operator values and are being handled separately.

**Verified**
`tsc --noEmit` clean; `lint-copy` clean; static export builds 18 routes. In the built
`out/index.html`: header contains `OperatorMark` and no `RiseLogo`, no "Authorized Reseller" tag,
disclosure text intact, brand `aria-label="Peak Connect home"`; footer `RiseLogo` labelled
"Rise Internet". Wordmark contrast 20.17:1 (strong) / 13.34:1 (light) over the hero and 15.6:1 /
9.55:1 on the scrolled bar. Reduced-motion 0 hidden elements; CLS 0.0016; 0 horizontal overflow
across 10 routes x 5 widths; plan CTAs 52px; sticky mobile call bar reveals correctly.

