## 2026-08-19 — MASTER STRUCTURE SPEC v1.2 conformance pass

**What changed**

Audited the build against the carrier-reseller master spec and implemented every gap. Grouped by
spec section.

**§2.0 / §2.1 — Top disclosure bar (was missing entirely)**
New `TopDisclosureBar` renders `Independent Authorized Reseller of Rise Internet® — Not Rise
Internet.` It is server-rendered, not dismissible, and nothing about it depends on hydration,
scroll position or a cookie choice.

It lives *inside* `SiteHeader`, above the nav row — not above the header in `layout.tsx`, which is
where it started. The header is `position: fixed; top: 0`, so a sibling bar above it was painted
over: the logo was clipped in half and the nav row lost most of its height. Nesting it in the
fixed header also means the disclosure is now permanently on screen rather than only at the top
of the page.

Consequence to remember: **the header's height is now variable.** The disclosure sentence wraps to
two lines under ~480px and three under ~380px, taking the header from 106px to ~140px. The hero's
top padding used a `vw`-based clamp, which *shrinks* exactly where the header *grows* — so the
hero eyebrow rendered underneath the header at 360–390px. Mobile padding is now a flat `8.5rem`,
with `10rem` below 430px. Any future change to that sentence must be re-measured at 360px.
`section[id] { scroll-margin-top }` was raised to `clamp(7.25rem, 9vw, 8rem)` for the same reason.

**§2 global — `data-call-cta` on every sales `tel:` link**
Was 15 tel: links, 0 with the attribute. Now every sales call link carries it, and §8.6 fires
conversions from one delegated listener on `[data-call-cta]` rather than per-button handlers — so
a new call button anywhere on the site is tracked the moment it ships.

Two deliberate exceptions, both correct: the carrier support number in the hero routing note and
in `service-fulfillment` link `tel:` but carry **no** `data-call-cta`. They are not sales leads;
firing a conversion on them would poison the call data. `service-fulfillment` also had a real bug
— the href was the reseller TFN while the label read the carrier's number. Fixed.

**§2.2 — Hero rebuilt as a phone-lead hero**
Added the disclosure eyebrow, and made tap-to-call the *primary* CTA with the number rendered as
visible text rather than hidden behind a verb. Added staffed-hours microcopy and "New orders only"
support routing so an existing customer is sent to the carrier instead of consuming a sales call.
The ZIP checker is demoted to a `<details>` — it cannot answer serviceability (the carrier
qualifies address by address) so it hands off rather than claiming a result it cannot know.

**§2.4 / §2.5 / §2.6 — three missing sections**
- `AddOns` (VAS): prices every add-on. Wi-Fi is rendered per-plan because its price genuinely
  differs by tier — free on 1 Gbps, half price on 500 Mbps, list on 150 Mbps.
- `FinePrint`: FCC-Broadband-Facts-style cost grid, split recurring / one-time / conditional.
  Every figure is verbatim from the carrier's Additional Fees disclosure (scrape-report §3).
  Deliberately the plainest block on the page — no photography, no entrance animation.
- `WhyOrderThroughUs`: why order through *this operator*, not why choose the carrier. Claims no
  exclusive pricing and no private discount, because there is none.

**§2.7 — How It Works cut from 4 steps to 3, ending in the call**
Step 2 was literally titled `A local technician surveys` — a §5.1 banned phrase. Restructured to
Call → We confirm plan and real cost → Technician installs, plus a closing call CTA.

**§2.8 — FAQ is now the last content section**
`FinalCta` moved above `FaqSection`. Running order is Hero → Plans → FinePrint → AddOns →
TrustBand → WhyOrderThroughUs → HowItWorks → FinalCta → FAQ.

**§2.9 / §7.5 — Footer**
Added the legal entity name and email (Google Misrepresentation wants all four of entity, address,
phone, email) and the trademark attribution line.

**§2.10 — Sticky mobile call bar (was missing)**
Appears after 520px of scroll so it never covers the hero's own CTA. Hidden above 900px, where the
header already keeps the number in view.

**§3 — Accessible price lockup**
New `PriceLockup`. The visual price row is `aria-hidden` and a generated `sr-only` sentence states
the same facts in prose — read literally, the old markup announced "49 dot 99 29 dot 99 slash m
o". Both halves are built from the same `plan` record so they cannot drift. Added the step-up
line: a visitor who misses that the rate is $20 higher without AutoPay has been shown half a price.

**§4 — Animation strip**
Removed, all named bans: Lenis smooth scroll, three.js, 3D tilt + glare cards, magnetic buttons,
the infinite marquee, pointer parallax, the animated mesh/aurora wash, Ken Burns drift, and the
scattered glowing dots and network-node clusters in the hero.

`HeroBackground` is now photograph + contrast scrim + static grain, with **no client JavaScript at
all**. GSAP was used in exactly one place after that, so `HowItWorks` was converted to Framer and
GSAP was uninstalled. Dependencies went from 7 to 5: framer-motion, next, react, react-dom.
**Measured effect: LCP 1024ms → 600ms.**

WARNING: this reverses several hero treatments requested earlier in the project (mesh gradient,
mouse parallax, glowing dots, network patterns). They were removed because the spec bans them by
name, not because they stopped working. Restoring any of them is a revert of `HeroBackground.tsx`
and its stylesheet.

Regression this caused, now fixed: `.ctaButton` on the plan cards inherited its appearance from
`MagneticButton`'s `size="lg"` tone classes. Deleting that component left the anchor unstyled at
40px tall. It now owns its styles and measures 52px.

**§5.1 / §5.3 — Copy linter**
New `scripts/lint-copy.mjs` + `scripts/lint-allowlist.txt`, wired into `npm run build` so a banned
phrase fails the build rather than shipping. Rules cover carrier-identity claims, unverifiable
superlatives, manufactured urgency, unsupportable service claims, and unreplaced placeholders.

Fixed the phrases it caught: `US-based` (x6, including page metadata), `No hidden fees`, and
`local technician`. Disclaimer copy that must *name* what it denies ("is not the official...") is
allowlisted with the narrowest possible substrings.

**§7.2 — Ninth legal page**
Added `/do-not-sell` (CPRA "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information"). The obligation is
triggered by the ad stack, not by intent: sharing identifiers with Google Ads is a "share" under
Cal. Civ. Code 1798.140(ah). No form on the page on purpose — this is a static export with no
server, so a form could not deliver a request. It offers GPC (honoured automatically) and email.

**§8.1 — Static export**
`output: 'export'`, `trailingSlash: true`, `images.unoptimized: true`. `robots.ts` and `sitemap.ts`
needed `export const dynamic = 'force-static'` or the build fails collecting page data. Build emits
18 prerendered routes.

**§8.3 — Added `public/llms.txt`** with plans, real total cost, and explicit qualifications for AI
systems (availability is not ZIP-derivable; no reviews exist, so any rating is fabricated).

**§8.6 — Consent Mode v2**
New `Analytics`. Consent defaults to granted (US-only funnel) in a `beforeInteractive` script so
the default is in the dataLayer before gtag.js loads, then downgrades on GPC or DNT. Inert until
`site.gtagId` is a real `AW-` id.

**§10 — FAQ 5 to 9 questions**, covering every required archetype. All nine already existed in
`faqLibrary`; only `FEATURED_IDS` changed, and `faqItems` still derives from it so the DOM and the
FAQPage schema cannot drift.

**Schema — `LocalBusiness` to `Organization`**
LocalBusiness asserts premises customers visit and makes the entity eligible for local-pack
placement. This is a telephone sales operation for someone else's network; claiming it would be
misrepresentation and would invite exactly the "is this the carrier's local office?" confusion the
disclosure architecture exists to prevent. Also fixed `openingHoursSpecification`, which claimed
00:00-23:59 while the line is staffed 8am-10pm.

**Files touched**
`src/lib/site.ts` (rewritten around §8.2 constants), `src/lib/fineprint.ts` (new),
`src/lib/{faq,nav,legalNav,plans,trust,schema}.ts`,
`src/components/compliance/{TopDisclosureBar,StickyCallBar,Analytics}.*` (new),
`src/components/sections/{FinePrint,AddOns,WhyOrderThroughUs}.*` (new),
`src/components/ui/PriceLockup.*` (new), `src/app/do-not-sell/page.tsx` (new),
`scripts/lint-copy.mjs` + `scripts/lint-allowlist.txt` (new), `public/llms.txt` (new),
`src/components/sections/{Hero,PlanGrid,HowItWorks,TrustBand,FinalCta}.*`,
`src/components/layout/{SiteHeader,SiteFooter}.*`, `src/app/{layout,page,robots,sitemap}.*`,
`src/app/globals.css`, `next.config.mjs`, `package.json`.

**Deleted** (all §4 bans or orphaned by earlier section removals): `SmoothScroll`, `VortexWebGL`,
`VortexField`, `VortexCanvas2D`, `HeroPlate`, `HeroAtmosphere`, `TiltCard`, `MagneticButton`,
`Marquee`, `Parallax`, `DrawPath`, `MeshSection`, `WhyRise`, `useMotionProfile`.

**Verified**
`tsc --noEmit` clean; `lint-copy` clean; static export builds 18 routes; LCP 600ms; CLS 0.0015;
reduced-motion 0 hidden elements; 0 horizontal overflow across 10 routes x 5 widths
(360/390/768/1024/1440); all sales `tel:` links carry `data-call-cta` and the two carrier support
links correctly do not; plan CTA 52px, all controls >= 24px (WCAG 2.5.8 AA).

**Two blockers the operator must resolve before any ad spend** — see the header comment in
`src/lib/site.ts`:
1. `entityLegalName` / address / email are placeholders. They must be the real registered entity
   and must match the Google Ads verified-advertiser identity string-for-string (§7.1).
2. `tfnDisplay` / `tfnE164` are placeholders. The number previously used site-wide,
   `1-844-411-7473`, is **Rise Internet's own published support line** — routing order calls there
   fails §12.4 (agents must answer with the reseller greeting) and poisons conversion data. §8.2
   requires a TFN unique to this site and program.

