## 2026-08-06 — Responsive verification pass; two real bugs fixed

**What changed**
Ran the site at 375 / 768 / 1024 / 1440 and fixed what the audit found.

- **Bug: mobile menu button was off-screen at 375px.** The header CTA was still rendering on
  phones, pushing the burger to x=408 in a 375px viewport — unreachable. Cause: `SiteHeader`'s
  `.cta { display: none }` and `MagneticButton`'s `.shell { display: inline-flex }` have equal
  specificity, so the later-loaded module won on source order. Additionally the button's wrapper
  `<span class="field">` was never targeted, so hiding the anchor alone would not have collapsed
  the layout. Fixed by wrapping the button in a header-owned `.ctaWrap` span and hiding that,
  which no other stylesheet can override. Also raised the hide threshold to 860px and reduced the
  wordmark size below 640px.
- **Bug: tablets were loading the WebGL scene.** The `compact` gate was `max-width: 767px`, so a
  768px tablet got the full Three.js particle scene. Added a separate `handheldQuery`
  (`max-width: 1024px`) and a `!coarse` condition used only for the WebGL gate, so tablets and
  touch devices now fall back to the 2D canvas. Layout breakpoints are unchanged.

**Files touched**
`src/components/layout/SiteHeader.tsx` · `SiteHeader.module.css` · `src/lib/useMotionProfile.ts`

**Verification**
- Horizontal overflow: none at any of the four widths (audit walks every element and ignores
  those inside `overflow-x` clipping ancestors, so the marquee track is correctly not counted).
- Canvas selection on fresh load: 375 → 2D, 768 → 2D, 1024 → 2D, 1440 → WebGL. Confirmed by
  probing whether the mounted canvas will yield a 2D context.
- Grid collapse: plans 3→2→1, install steps 4→2→1, mesh features 4→3→2→1, footer 4→2→1.
- Header nav swaps to the burger drawer at ≤1100px; burger sits fully inside the viewport at 375.
- FAQ accordion: 18 items, first open by default, `aria-expanded` toggles correctly and opening
  one closes the other.
- Reduced-motion guard confirmed present in the shipped stylesheet:
  `[data-reveal] { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; clip-path: none !important; }`
  across 17 revealed elements.
- SSR HTML (no JS) contains all three prices, the AutoPay disclaimer, the reseller disclosure and
  the full JSON-LD graph — the page is fully crawlable without executing any animation code.
- All 8 legal routes return HTTP 200 with 2,000–3,500 words each.
- No console errors. `tsc --noEmit` clean, `next build` green, 14/14 static.

