## 2026-08-06 — Legal routes, SEO surface, first green build

**What changed**
Authored the eight reseller policy pages as real routes with full substantive content (no
placeholder text), added the SEO/crawl surface, and got the project to a clean production build.

- Built `LegalShell`, a shared chrome for policy pages: header with breadcrumb + last-updated,
  prose styling, sibling-policy sidebar, contact block.
- Wrote all eight policies with genuine content:
  - `/disclaimer` — reseller status, Rise Broadband → Rise Internet rename, pricing accuracy,
    speed-claim limits, availability caveats, liability limitation.
  - `/trademarks` — nominative fair use rationale, third-party mark attribution (Rise, eero,
    Wi-Fi Alliance), no-endorsement statement, rights-holder contact route.
  - `/privacy-policy` — collection/use/sharing/retention, CCPA-style rights incl. appeal, GPC
    honoured, explicit "we never collect SSN/DOB/card data" carve-out.
  - `/cookies-policy` — three categories with per-cookie purpose/duration tables, consent
    controls, GPC.
  - `/tcpa-policy` — prior express written consent mechanics, calling hours, STOP/HELP, internal
    DNC list with 10-business-day/5-year commitments.
  - `/marketing-policy` — advertising standards, incl. an explicit no-manufactured-urgency rule
    and a no-fabricated-reviews rule.
  - `/service-fulfillment` — the full order→install→cancel lifecycle plus the complete published
    fee table.
  - `/pci-dss` — out-of-scope position (we never touch card data) and the controls we hold anyway.
- Added `sitemap.ts`, `robots.ts`, and a branded `not-found.tsx`.
- Added `.claude/launch.json` for the dev server.

**Files touched**
`src/components/layout/LegalShell.tsx` · `LegalShell.module.css` ·
`src/app/{disclaimer,trademarks,privacy-policy,cookies-policy,tcpa-policy,marketing-policy,service-fulfillment,pci-dss}/page.tsx` ·
`src/app/sitemap.ts` · `src/app/robots.ts` · `src/app/not-found.tsx` · `.claude/launch.json`

**Why**
Step 3 required eight separate legal routes with real content, and required `/disclaimer` and
`/trademarks` to state the independent-reseller position explicitly. Ad platforms check
destination pages for exactly this, so thin or templated policy text would have been a liability
rather than a formality.

**Verification** — `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `npx next build` succeeds, 14/14 routes prerendered
static. Home first-load JS 213 kB with Three.js correctly excluded (lazy chunk).

