## 2026-08-06 — Page build: sections, motion system, hero WebGL

**What changed**
Built the single-page site and the animation layer.

- **Token architecture** (`globals.css`) — original naming scheme, deliberately not a mirror of
  the source site's variable structure: `--ember-*` (brand), `--ink-*`, `--pane-*`, `--rule-*`,
  `--lift-*` (elevation), `--wash-*` (gradients), `--flow-*` (motion), `--bend-*` (radii),
  `--step-*` (spacing), `--type-*` (fluid type), `--tier-*` (z-ladder).
- **Capability gate** (`useMotionProfile.ts`) — single source of truth for reduced-motion, coarse
  pointer, compact viewport, WebGL availability and low-power heuristics. Every animated component
  reads from it rather than sniffing independently, so fallbacks stay consistent.
- **Motion primitives** — `RevealText` (word/char stagger through an overflow mask, full string
  exposed to AT via sr-only), `Reveal`, `Parallax`, `ClipWipe`, `StaggerGrid`/`StaggerItem`,
  `MagneticButton` (shell and label track at different strengths for parallax depth), `TiltCard`
  (spring-smoothed 3D tilt + pointer-tracking glare), `DrawPath` (scrubbed SVG stroke draw of a
  fixed-wireless relay topology), `Marquee` (duplicated track, -50% translate for a seamless seam).
- **Lenis + GSAP** (`SmoothScroll.tsx`) — Lenis registered with `ScrollTrigger.scrollerProxy`,
  driven off GSAP's ticker so both libraries share one clock; anchor clicks routed through Lenis.
  Disabled entirely under reduced motion.
- **Hero ambient** — `VortexWebGL` (2,600-point GPU-animated spiral, additive blend, accretion
  ring, IntersectionObserver + visibility pausing, DPR capped at 1.75) with `VortexCanvas2D`
  fallback (140 particles, 30fps throttle, DPR 1.5). `VortexField` picks between them; renders
  nothing during SSR so it can never delay LCP.
- **Sections** — Hero (address check + reseller disclosure near hero), PlanGrid (tilt cards),
  TrustBand (marquee + crawlable state list), MeshSection (eero 7 specs + 7 features), HowItWorks
  (scroll-scrubbed 4-card assembly + SVG draw), WhyRise (count-up stats), FaqSection (accordion),
  FinalCta. Header with scroll-reactive chrome and clip-path mobile drawer; footer with full nav.
- **Structured data** (`schema.ts`) — one `@graph`: LocalBusiness, WebSite, BreadcrumbList, three
  Product/Offer records, FAQPage.

**Files touched**
`src/app/{layout,page,globals.css}` · `src/lib/{site,plans,trust,faq,mesh,legalNav,schema,useMotionProfile}.ts` ·
`src/components/motion/*` · `src/components/hero/*` · `src/components/sections/*` ·
`src/components/layout/{SiteHeader,SiteFooter}.tsx` · `src/components/ui/AddressCheck.tsx`

**Why**
Steps 2, 4 and 5. Two decisions are worth recording because they are not obvious from the code:

1. **No testimonials section.** The source site publishes no reviews anywhere. Rather than invent
   reviewer names and dates, that slot carries a marquee of sourced facts and the published
   coverage footprint. `schema.ts` deliberately omits `AggregateRating`/`Review` for the same
   reason.
2. **No urgency copy anywhere.** The struck-through plan prices are the ongoing $20 AutoPay
   discount, not a limited-time promotion — `listPrice - price === 20` on all three tiers. The
   source publishes no expiry date or intro term, so none is asserted. `plans.ts` carries a
   comment warning against adding one.

