## 2026-08-06 — Step 1: source scrape and extraction

**What changed**
Scraped risebroadband.com and extracted design tokens, pricing and content before writing any code.

- Discovered the site **301-redirects to riseinternet.com** — the brand was renamed from Rise
  Broadband to Rise Internet. Legacy `rise-broadband-*` slugs survive in legal URLs, confirming a
  rebrand rather than a domain change.
- Bot protection required a real headless-browser render: `sitemap.xml` returns 403 to plain
  clients and same-origin `fetch()` returns a 202 challenge. All data came from genuine navigation
  of the hydrated DOM.
- Extracted the live token system from computed CSS custom properties: brand ramp (`#ff5601` core),
  neutrals, gradients, the Barlow / Barlow Condensed / Barlow Semi Condensed superfamily with
  loaded weights, fluid type scale, spacing, radii, the 4-stop float shadow, and motion easings.
- Captured plans verbatim from the homepage and `/compare-plans`, the eero 7 spec sheet and
  disclaimer from `/advanced-wifi`, all 24 Q&As from `/faqs`, trust figures from `/about`, the
  10-state footprint from `/areas-we-serve`, and the complete fee schedule from
  `/legal/additional-fees-disclosure-statement`.

**Files touched** `docs/scrape-report.md`

**Why**
Step 1 required showing extraction before building. The report also documents eight items that
could **not** be confirmed and must not be invented — most importantly the total absence of
customer reviews on the source site, the absence of any promotional end date, and the absence of
separate fixed-wireless vs fiber pricing.

