## 2026-08-07 — Hero background image and reseller lockup

**What changed**

- **Hero background image.** Copied the supplied fibre-optic render to
  `src/assets/hero-fiber.jpg` (2752×1536) and set it as the hero plate via `next/image` with a
  static import — `fill`, `priority`, `sizes="100vw"`, `quality={82}`, `placeholder="blur"`. The
  static import supplies intrinsic dimensions so the box is reserved and the image contributes no
  CLS; `priority` makes it the LCP fetch rather than a lazy one. Next serves AVIF/WebP and
  resolution-matched widths (1920 at desktop, 1280 at laptop).
  `object-position: 68% 50%` biases the frame right, because the fibre convergence sits
  right-of-centre in the source while the copy occupies the left.
- **Contrast scrim reworked.** The old radial ember veil became a left-weighted linear scrim over
  `rgb(9 12 20)`, so type stays legible over the copy column while the fibre detail survives on the
  right. Tuned against measured values rather than by eye: composited the scrim over real image
  pixels on a canvas and sampled a grid under each text block. First pass gave a 4.23:1 worst case
  on the headline; raising the mid stops (0.62→0.72 at 52%, 0.34→0.48 at 76%) brought it to
  **5.47:1** on a 110px headline (AA-large needs 3) with the lede at **12.75:1**.
  Phones get a flat vertical scrim instead, since copy spans the full width there — measured
  **12.98:1** headline / **12.17:1** lede at 375px.
- **"Authorized Reseller" lockup** added beside the wordmark in both the header and the footer,
  set on two lines behind a vertical rule so it reads as a qualifier on the brand rather than part
  of the mark. Header inherits `currentColor` so it flips with the scrolled state.
  The initial mobile override shrank it to 8px; measurement showed 151px of slack in the bar at
  375px, so the override now only tightens spacing and holds the type at 10px — it is a
  disclosure, and 8px is too small to function as one.

