## 2026-08-07 — Hero atmosphere (GSAP + Framer Motion) and a reduced-motion visibility fix

**What changed**

- **`components/hero/HeroAtmosphere.tsx` (new)** — the animated layer over the background plate:
  - *Gradient glows* (Framer Motion): three drifting radial orbs on 22s/27s/14s loops. Ember and
    cyan use `mix-blend-mode: screen` so they read as light in the scene; a third deep-blue orb sits
    behind the headline on `normal` blend, adding depth without lifting luminance under the type.
  - *Network constellation* (GSAP): 14 nodes / 18 edges, hand-authored in a 600×600 viewBox and
    weighted right so it never reaches the copy column, with a gradient mask fading its left edge.
    Edges draw in via per-line `getTotalLength()` dash offsets; nodes breathe on offset sine loops;
    7 data pulses run the edges. Segments are straight, so a linear cx/cy tween traces them exactly
    and MotionPathPlugin is not needed. Timings come from a deterministic `sin`-based jitter so the
    field varies without `Math.random()` (which would break SSR and GSAP resume).
  - *Sheen*: a slow skewed light sweep across the plate.
- **Hero scroll parallax (GSAP ScrollTrigger)** — plate drifts at 18% (8% on phones) with a 1.06
  scale, atmosphere at 26%, copy lifts −12% and fades, all on one scrubbed timeline. `.plate` is
  bled `-12%` vertically so the travel never exposes an edge.
- **Hero entrance (Framer Motion)** — lede and address form fade up on a stagger. The **h1 is
  deliberately transform-only with no opacity fade**: it is the LCP element, and an element at
  `opacity: 0` is not counted as painted, so fading it in would push LCP out by the transition
  duration.
- Layer order is `plate(-4) → atmos(-3) → veil(-2)`. The atmosphere sits **beneath** the contrast
  scrim by design, so none of it disturbs the previously measured headline contrast.

**Two bugs found by verification and fixed**

1. *Pulse circles rendered without `cx`/`cy`*, so SVG threw
   `attribute cx: Unexpected end of attribute` on every frame until GSAP's first tick. Now seeded
   in JSX at their edge's start node.
2. *Reduced-motion content was invisible.* `StaggerGrid`/`StaggerItem`/`Reveal`/`ClipWipe`/
   `RevealText` branched on `useReducedMotion()`, which returns null during SSR and a boolean after
   hydration. The server emitted Framer's `opacity: 0` initial style while the client rendered an
   unstyled element; React does not patch up mismatched attributes, so `opacity: 0` persisted —
   **all three plan cards and every mesh feature tile were permanently invisible for
   reduced-motion users**, the exact audience the fallback exists for. All five components now
   render identical markup regardless, and reduced motion is enforced solely by the
   `[data-reveal], [data-motion]` rule in globals.css. Measured invisible elements: **11 → 1**, and
   the remaining one is the intentional `.sr-only` heading.

**Files touched**
`src/components/hero/HeroAtmosphere.tsx` (new), `HeroAtmosphere.module.css` (new),
`src/components/sections/Hero.tsx`, `Hero.module.css`,
`src/components/motion/StaggerGrid.tsx`, `Reveal.tsx`, `ClipWipe.tsx`, `RevealText.tsx`,
`src/app/globals.css`

**Verification**
The in-app Browser pane could not be used — it is not displayed, so its tab is `document.hidden`
with **0 rAF ticks**, which suspends GSAP and Framer Motion entirely and makes animation
unobservable there. Verified instead by driving the cached Playwright chromium headlessly
(`scratchpad/verify-hero.mjs`, `verify-reduced.mjs`) at 1440/1024/375 plus a reduced-motion pass:
31 rAF ticks per 500ms in all runs; 18/18 edges drawn, glows/nodes/pulses all confirmed changing
between samples, parallax matrix confirmed on scroll (93.7px desktop, 41.7px mobile); mobile
correctly omits the constellation; reduced-motion pass has every animation off. Zero hydration
errors and zero SVG attribute errors across all four runs. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

**Known gap**
`/favicon.ico`, `/icon.png` and `/apple-icon.png` all 404 — the one remaining console error.
Not addressed; out of scope for this change.

