## 2026-08-07 — Hero reduced to the bare artwork

**What changed**

Stripped the hero back to the image alone, per instruction: no animations, no glass/blur, no zoom,
nothing layered over the picture.

- **`Hero.tsx` rewritten as a static server component.** Removed `HeroPlate` (3D deck, pointer
  tilt, spotlight, glints, blurred back plane), `HeroAtmosphere` (glows, constellation, sheen), the
  GSAP ScrollTrigger parallax timeline, and the Framer Motion entrance animations. It now holds one
  `next/image` and the copy. No hooks, so only AddressCheck ships JS from this section.
- **Removed every overlay**: the `.veil` contrast scrim (both the left wash and the lower-left
  pool), the `.atmos` layer, the bottom `.fade`, and the header's gradient shim.
- **No crop or zoom.** `.plate` is `inset: 0` with no bleed or transform, and the section is pinned
  to the artwork's own `aspect-ratio: 2752 / 1536`, so the image renders at its native framing.
  Below 900px the ratio is dropped (it would leave the section far too short for the copy) and the
  image covers the content height instead.
- Legibility now rests entirely on `text-shadow` applied to the type itself — headline, lede, note,
  nav links, phone, reseller tag — plus a `drop-shadow` filter on the logo so the SVG bolt gets it
  too. All of these clear when the header turns solid on scroll.

**Files touched**
`src/components/sections/Hero.tsx`, `Hero.module.css`,
`src/components/layout/SiteHeader.module.css`

`HeroPlate.tsx/.module.css` and `HeroAtmosphere.tsx/.module.css` are now unreferenced. Left on disk
rather than deleted; they are no longer imported, so they are not bundled.

**Verification**
`tsc --noEmit` clean. Image renders whole and at full brightness (peak luma 255, bright-pixel share
21.6% desktop / 25.0% mobile). Nav links measure 5.05–12.07:1 on text-shadow alone.

**Known defect — reported to the user, not silently accepted**
With the artwork shown whole and nothing layered over it, the bright fibre bundle now sweeps
through the middle-left where the body copy sits. Measured against the rendered background:
headline **1.54:1**, lede **1.20:1** desktop; **1.2 / 1.1** mobile. WCAG AA needs 3:1 for large
text and 4.5:1 for body. The lede's lower half is genuinely hard to read, which the screenshot
confirms. The reseller tag (3.84:1) and header phone number (3.83:1) also sit under 4.5.
Text-shadow raises perceived legibility but does not count toward the WCAG ratio and cannot rescue
white type over a near-white background. This is an unavoidable consequence of "show the whole
image" plus "no layer over it" — the artwork has no dark region large enough to hold the full copy
block. Options put to the user rather than chosen unilaterally.

**Decision (user, 2026-08-07): leave as is.**
The contrast shortfall above is accepted deliberately. The artwork stays full-frame, at native
ratio, at full brightness, with nothing layered over it — that is the priority for this hero, and
the lede's readability is knowingly traded for it.

DO NOT "fix" this by reintroducing a scrim, gradient, blur or overlay on the hero image. Four
options were put to the user (move copy below the image, crop back to the dark area, small scrim
behind the lede only, leave as is) and "leave as is" was chosen explicitly. Treat any overlay on
this hero as a regression unless the user asks for one.

Remaining known gaps, unchanged: headline 1.54:1 / lede 1.20:1 desktop, 1.2 / 1.1 mobile; reseller
tag 3.84:1; header phone 3.83:1. Also still open from earlier sessions: no favicon (/favicon.ico,
/icon.png, /apple-icon.png all 404), and no fee disclaimer adjacent to the advertised prices.

