## 2026-08-07 — Advanced Wi-Fi section: layout, typography, and a ClipWipe deadlock

**Root cause of the "empty space on the right"**
The right column was not empty by design — it held the eero 7 spec card, which was **invisible and
always had been**. `ClipWipe` put `whileInView` and its own closed clip-path on the same element.
`inset(0% 0% 0% 100%)` collapses the visible box to zero width, so IntersectionObserver reported
`isIntersecting: false` at every scroll position, so the animation that would have opened it never
fired. Measured `intersectionRatio: 0` even with the card scrolled to viewport centre.

`ClipWipe` now splits the two: an unclipped outer wrapper owns the viewport trigger and propagates
a variant to the clipped child. Verified opening to `inset(0%)` on scroll. This affected only this
one instance — it is the only ClipWipe on the site — but the component was broken for any caller.

**Layout and typography** (`MeshSection.module.css`)
- `.top` was `grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr` with `.intro` capped at `46ch`, which resolved
  to **416px**. A 68px headline in a 416px column is what produced the four near-one-word lines.
  `.top` is now a single full-width flex column; the spec card sits beneath the intro rather than
  beside it.
- `.heading`: `max-width: 56rem`, `line-height: 1.06`, `letter-spacing: var(--track-crush)`.
  Resolves to **2 lines at every breakpoint** (1440 / 1280 / 1024 / 768 / 375), down from 4.
- `.lede`: `clamp(1.125rem, 0.6vw + 1rem, 1.375rem)` (22px desktop → 18.25px mobile),
  `line-height: var(--lead-relaxed)`, `max-width: 48rem`, and colour `#a1a1aa` — a cool neutral
  grey against the pure-white headline rather than dimmed white. 6.7:1 on this background.
- `.specList` became a 3-column grid (2 at ≤720px, 1 at ≤480px) with each spec as a label-over-
  value pair on an ember rule, since it is now full width rather than a narrow sidebar list.
- `.specBadge` ("eero 7"): white on `#ff5601` measured **3.19:1** at 12px. Switched the text to
  `--ink-strong` on the same orange for **5.58:1**, so the badge keeps its brightness.

**Verification**
40 text runs in the section audited against rendered pixels: 1 remaining failure, and it is the
already-reported CTA gradient issue below. Headline 2 lines and zero horizontal overflow at all
five breakpoints. Spec card confirmed `inset(0%)` (open). `tsc --noEmit` clean.

**Still outstanding, unchanged**
White on the primary CTA gradient measures 3.06:1 here (2.64:1 against its lightest stop).
Reported previously; not changed, because darkening `--wash-cta` affects every primary button.

