## 2026-08-07 — Real photography wired into six sections

**What changed**

Nine delivered images implemented, plus OG card and favicons.

| Image | Placement |
|---|---|
| `hero-family.jpeg` | Hero background — replaced `hero-fiber.jpg` |
| `coverage-family.jpeg` | TrustBand background (new `.plate` + light scrim) |
| `wifi-household.jpeg` | Advanced Wi-Fi background (new `.plate` + `.plateScrim`) |
| `step-1..4-*.jpeg` | Four How-it-works cards — new 4:3 `.shot` bleeding to the card edge, subtle hover zoom; step numeral reduced since the photo now leads |
| `support-agent.jpeg` | FAQ sticky panel — new `<figure>` with a gradient caption strip |
| `cta-household.jpeg` | Final CTA — under the brand orange at 0.58 opacity, `mix-blend-mode: multiply` |
| `opengraph-image.jpeg` | Moved to `src/app/` — Next file convention |
| `icon.jpeg` + `apple-icon.jpeg` | Moved/copied to `src/app/` |

All wired as `next/image` static imports with `placeholder="blur"`, per-slot `sizes`, and
per-slot `quality` (74–90). Only the hero keeps `priority`.

`isolation: isolate` added to `.section` in MeshSection so the new negative-z children stack
above the section background rather than behind it.

**Contrast fixes this forced**
- Final CTA lede measured **4.02:1** (white at 0.88 alpha over brand orange — it was already
  failing before the image at ~3.16:1). Solid white plus raising the plate to 0.58 took it to
  **4.99:1**; the headline is **5.57:1**.
- FAQ caption measured **2.94:1** over the lit part of the portrait. Its gradient now ramps from
  40% instead of fading linearly — **9.35:1**.

**Verification**
All 9 images load, zero HTTP failures, zero console errors, zero horizontal overflow.
**LCP 1304ms, CLS 0.** OG and icon metadata confirmed emitted in `<head>`. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

**Measurement note for future sessions**
Two probe techniques give false failures here and cost time twice: (1) resolving background via
`getComputedStyle().backgroundColor` returns transparent for gradients and walks up to a white
ancestor — the CTA "1.00:1" readings are bogus; (2) sampling an element's *layout box* includes
padding where an overlay gradient is still transparent. Use `Range.getClientRects()` on the text
node and sample the rendered screenshot. `scratchpad/pixel2.mjs` does this correctly.

**Deliberately not implemented**
Plan-card thumbnails. Those cards already carry speed, two prices, a discount note, three spec
rows, a blurb and a CTA; photos push the buttons below the laptop fold on the page's highest-value
block. Prompts remain in `docs/image-plan.md` if that call is revisited.

