## 2026-08-07 — Advanced Wi-Fi: contrast, frost panel, defined feature cards

**Root problem in the reference screenshot:** the `wifi-household` background was showing straight
through the feature cards. Their fill was `rgb(255 255 255 / 0.03)` — a 3% white tint over a
photograph — so card edges dissolved and the body copy sat on lit interior.

**What changed** (`MeshSection.module.css`, plus one element in the tsx)

- **Feature cards are now opaque** `#101012` with an orange inner-glow border
  (`inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(255 138 62 / 0.06)` + `border: 1px solid rgb(255 138 62 / 0.22)`), lifting
  to a `0 0 24px rgb(255 86 1 / 0.14)` bloom on hover. Titles moved to `--ember-lift` orange, body
  copy to solid `#ced1d8` instead of 48%-alpha white — the alpha version let the photo bleed
  through the glyphs. Icon tiles gained a border and inner ember glow. Seven cards, 4-up grid.
- **Spec card rebuilt as real frost:** `backdrop-filter: blur(26px) saturate(1.5)` over a
  **dark-tinted** base (`rgb(24 24 28 / 0.72) → rgb(12 12 15 / 0.82)`). A white translucent fill
  was the obvious choice and the wrong one — over a lit interior it pushed the right-hand stat
  boxes to 4.07:1 and 2.97:1. Tinting dark keeps the glass read and restores contrast.
- **Six stat boxes** are now bordered containers with their own 6px backdrop blur: labels
  uppercase `#b9bcc4` micro, values `--ember-lift` orange at 800.
- **Ember particle field** (`.particles`) — eight small orange radial dots on a 22s drift,
  `animation: none` under reduced motion.
- **Scrim retuned twice.** First pass (0.96→0.82 horizontal plus a vertical pass) killed the
  interior entirely — a black void, not the requested depth. Final values are directional:
  0.93 at the left to protect the headline and lede, falling to 0.38 at the right so the interior
  reads through. That only works *because* the cards and panel are now opaque and carry their own
  contrast.

**Verification**
40 text runs audited against rendered pixels: **1 failure**, the pre-existing CTA gradient
(3.06:1 "Check availability"). Everything in the panel and cards passes. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

