## 2026-08-07 — Cross-route nav from legal pages; plan CTAs to "Call now"

**Nav from legal routes**
`primaryNav` hrefs are hash-only (`#plans`), which resolve to nothing on a legal page — those
sections do not exist there, so clicking did nothing. `SiteHeader` now reads `usePathname()`:
on `/` the links stay hash-only so the Lenis handler in `SmoothScroll` intercepts and scrolls
smoothly; off `/` they render as `next/link` to `/#plans` and route properly. Applies to both the
desktop nav and the mobile drawer. The logo already pointed at `/` and was fine.

Added `scroll-margin-top: clamp(5.25rem, 7vw, 6rem)` on `section[id]` in globals.css. Without it a
cross-route hash lands the section flush at y=0, behind the fixed header — the heading was hidden.
Lenis applies its own `-88` offset for same-page clicks, but a hash arriving via route change is
handled natively and gets no offset. Verified: sections now land at **96px**, clear of the bar.

**Plan CTAs**
All three plan cards swapped from "Check availability" to "Call now" with a phone glyph, linking to
`site.salesPhoneHref`. Each carries a distinct `aria-label` naming the number and the plan, so
screen-reader users do not get three identical "Call now" links.

This required a fix in `MagneticButton`: it routed every `href` through `next/link`, which is for
client-side navigation and would intercept `tel:`. It now renders a plain `<a>` when the href has a
protocol (`tel:`, `mailto:`, external `http`) and `next/link` otherwise.

**Verification**
From `/privacy-policy`, each of the four nav items navigates to `/` and lands on its own section
(`plans`, `advanced-wifi`, `how-it-works`, `faq` each at 96px). Logo returns `/`. On `/` the hrefs
revert to hash-only. Plan CTAs confirmed rendering as `<a href="tel:18444117473">`. Zero console
errors, `tsc --noEmit` clean.

