## 2026-08-07 — Section differentiation pass

**Problem:** PlanGrid and HowItWorks were both white rounded cards in an equal grid with the same
scale-and-fade stagger; FAQ was a generic light accordion. Three sections read as one template.

**How it works — card grid → full-bleed alternating rows**
No container, no cards, no borders, no shadows. Each step is a photograph bleeding to the viewport
edge with copy on the facing side; sides swap every row. Numerals are oversized and *outlined*
(`-webkit-text-stroke`) rather than filled badges. Head is a two-column split with the second line
in a quieter grey. Entrance is a **split reveal** — the photo unclips from the outer edge while the
copy slides in from the opposite direction — driven by per-row ScrollTriggers with `once: true`,
replacing the previous scattered scrub-assembly.

**Plans — equal grid → asymmetric offset**
Columns are now `0.92fr / 1.16fr / 0.92fr`: the recommended plan is wider and sits flush while the
flanking two drop by `clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem)`. Cards are **borderless and floating**
(`--lift-float`, no border, `--bend-xl`) instead of hairline-bordered. Section background is tinted
with an ember radial rather than plain white. Head is centred; the heading stacks three lines with
the middle in `--ember-press`. Entrance dropped `StaggerGrid` for a per-card **clip wipe from the
bottom** on a **centre-out** delay (`[0.16, 0, 0.16]`) — the featured card lands first.

**FAQ — light accordion → dark, numbered, reversed**
Section is now dark with an ember radial. Columns reversed: the list leads on the **left** and the
sticky head sits on the **right** (`order`), the inverse of every other section. Each question
carries a tabular `01`–`05` index instead of an icon tile. All surfaces retuned for the dark panel.

**TrustBand — oversized figures added**
`trustStats` (21+ years, 4.2M households, 10 states, 24/7) were orphaned when Why Rise was removed
— the strongest trust signals on the page were rendering nowhere. They are back as four
hairline-divided columns of display numerals, no cards or tiles.

**Contrast failures this introduced, both fixed**
- "One afternoon." used `--ink-faint` (#b3b3b3) → **2.10:1** on white, under the 3:1 large-text
  floor even at 80px. Moved to `--ink-mute` (5.28:1).
- The FAQ eyebrow's `--ember-text` measured **3.98:1** against the new dark panel. Moved to
  `--ember-lift`.

**Verification**
Page-wide contrast: 0 real failures. The two remaining reported (`FinalCTA` headline, FAQ portrait
caption) are the known gradient-background false positives — both verified by pixel measurement
earlier at 5.57:1 and 9.35:1. Responsive audit across 9 routes × 5 widths: **no issues**.
Warm **LCP 1160ms, CLS 0**. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

