## 2026-08-07 — Plan card corners + hover states

**Cut corners**
`clip-path: inset(0%)` still clips to a sharp rectangle, so after the wipe finished it was squaring
off the cards' `--bend-xl` corners and slicing their drop shadow — visible as notched bottom
corners. The `shown` variant now carries `transitionEnd: { clipPath: 'none' }`, releasing the clip
once the animation completes. `.wipe` also got bottom padding (with a negative margin to keep
layout unchanged) so the shadow has somewhere to live while the clip is still active mid-wipe.
Verified: all three resolve to `clip-path: none` after entry.

**Hover**
- `.card::after` — ember ring (`inset 0 0 0 1.5px` + a soft 4px outer halo), fading in on hover.
  The featured card gets a white-tinted variant so the ring reads against its orange fill.
- `.card::before` — warm bloom rising from the base, blurred 28px.
- Lift raised from 6px to 8px with `--lift-deep`.
- Speed figure warms to `--ember-press` (4.56:1 on white, passes at display size) and the unit
  nudges up 3px on `--ease-pop`.
- Spec divider rules brighten to `--ember-haze` as a set.

**Measurement note**
`[class*="card"]` is ambiguous — TiltCard and PlanGrid both define a `.card` class, and the
TiltCard wrapper comes first in the DOM. An initial probe reported the ring at opacity 1 at rest
and the speed colour unchanged on hover; both were the selector matching the wrong element. Scope
to the module-prefixed name (`[class*="PlanGrid_card"]`) when probing these.

**Verification**
Responsive clean; page contrast unchanged. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

