## 2026-08-07 — Network clusters made visible; CountUp fixed

**Network clusters** were already present but at `opacity: 0.5` with a `0.09` stroke — effectively
invisible. Now three clusters (14 nodes, 14 edges): two in the dark left corner, one centre-frame.
Layer opacity 0.9, stroke 0.16, and the mask holds full strength to 62% so the centre cluster is no
longer dimmed. Split L7 / C7 confirmed.

Nodes moved out of the SVG into positioned elements. The streams SVG uses
`preserveAspectRatio="none"` so its lines span the box correctly, but that same non-uniform scale
turns `<circle>` into an ellipse — the nodes were rendering as horizontal ovals.

**CountUp (TrustBand) — two bugs from the previous session, both fixed**
1. *Counts stalled near zero* (figures read "2+", "0.3M"). The effect depended on the regex `match`
   array, which is a new object every render, so it re-ran continuously and reset `start` before
   the animation could advance. Now depends on extracted primitives (`target`, `suffix`,
   `decimals`).
2. *Hydration error under reduced motion.* The initial render seeded `0`, but `useReducedMotion()`
   returns null during SSR and a boolean after, so server and client disagreed. State now
   initialises to the finished value, so both render the same thing and the count only starts
   post-mount.

Frame-by-frame capture confirms the roll: `10+ → 18+ → 20+ → 21+` over ~900ms, settling on
21+ / 4.2M / 10 / 24/7.

**Selector trap, again:** `[class*="netNode"]` also matches the container `netNodes`, which
reported the layer as a 1440×803 "node" and made the roundness check fail. Same class as the
`[class*="card"]` / TiltCard collision. Use the `__hash` suffix (`[class*="netNode__"]`).

**Verification** All 14 nodes round and pulsing; frozen under reduced motion; zero console errors.
Contrast desktop headline **17.9:1**, lede **16.82:1**; mobile headline 5.98:1 (floor is 3:1 at
that size). Responsive clean. `tsc --noEmit` clean.

