## 2026-08-07 — ZIP-only availability field; ember glow on the light sections

**Availability input is now a ZIP field, not a free-text address box**
`AddressCheck` changed beyond the placeholder, because a placeholder swap alone would have left a
street-address autofill and a full keyboard on mobile:
- `placeholder` → "Enter your ZIP code"; `<label>` and the success message updated to match
- `autoComplete` `street-address` → `postal-code`
- `inputMode` `text` → `numeric` (numeric keypad on mobile)
- `pattern="[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?"`, `maxLength={10}`
- Validation moved from a length>=4 check to `/^\d{5}(-\d{4})?$/`, so ZIP+4 is accepted and
  anything else is rejected with "Enter a 5-digit ZIP code…"

Verified: invalid input surfaces the error, `80202` returns the confirmation.

**Ember glow on the light sections**
- `PlanGrid`: three positioned radials on the section plus a wide blurred `::before` ellipse
  (`blur(90px)`) behind the cards. Section children lifted to `z-index: 1` so the wash stays
  behind them.
- `HowItWorks`: was flat `--pane-base`. Now two corner radials plus a blurred ember band under the
  rail. `isolation: isolate` + `overflow: hidden` so the `::before` cannot escape the section.

Both are warm-light washes, not shapes — heavy blur and low alpha, keyed to `--ember-core` /
`--ember-lift`.

**Verification** Contrast: 0 real failures (the four HowItWorks numerals reported at 1.13:1 are the
known false positive — the script resolves the section background instead of the photo behind them;
`num.mjs` measures them at 3.89–14.14:1). **LCP 1024ms, CLS 0.0001.** Responsive clean across 9
routes × 5 widths. `tsc --noEmit` clean.
